 {:id "adr-2607105000-kotoba-lang-standard-model-hypercharge-generator-bug-fix"
  :title "ADR-2607105000: kotoba-lang/standard-model — extending independent-review discipline to the original 6 namespaces finds and fixes a real hypercharge-normalization bug"
  :status "accepted"
  :date "2026-07-10"
  :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"]
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model"
  :authoritative true
  :authoritative_for
  ["extends this session's GTG-proven independent-adversarial-review
    discipline (re-derive from physics literature before reading code) to
    the ORIGINAL 6 namespaces (kotoba.sm.complex/tensor/vector-field/spinor/
    gauge/standard-model, ADR-2607051500), which had never received this
    intensity of review despite predating and being independent of GTG"
   "landed 2026-07-09/10: kotoba-lang/standard-model#15 merged as
    519e5da8daff98692a720538e50506ea8848c50f, 80 tests/2918 assertions
    (up from 79/2911), CI green JDK17+21; superproject pin advanced via API
    single-entry commit df6500d3629421e57c5f2741d48def5af1d52b65"
   "BUG: covariant-derivative-sm built the U(1)_Y gauge generator from raw
    fermion hypercharge :Y, not :Y/2. This namespace's own GMN convention
    (Q=T3+Y/2, already correctly checked by gell-mann-nishijima-ok?) requires
    Y/2. After electroweak mixing (via this namespace's own mixing-matrix/
    photon-Z inverted), photon coupling = e*(T3+Y_eff) since
    e=g*sin(theta_W)=g'*cos(theta_W) (independently satisfied by this
    namespace's own mass/mixing functions) -- equals required e*Q=e*(T3+Y/2)
    only for Y_eff=Y/2. Raw Y gives e*(T3+Y), wrong for every charged
    fermion with T3!=0 -- 50% too large in magnitude for e_L specifically
    (T3=-1/2,Y=-1: (T3+Y)/(T3+Y/2)=1.5)"
   "why undetected at original landing: the only test of
    covariant-derivative-sm exercised exclusively the fields-off case, where
    U(1) generator normalization cannot matter. No test decomposed the
    combined SU(2)/U(1) output into the physical photon direction and
    checked against e*Q -- classic each-piece-verified-in-isolation gap"
   "requester independently re-verified before merge: re-derived
    e*(T3+Y_eff)=e*Q algebra from scratch, and while building an even
    stronger regression test caught+fixed a coupling-constant argument-order
    mistake in that test's OWN first draft (passing gw=1.0 instead of g)
    before it could land a subtly-wrong passing test -- same
    verify-the-verification discipline applied throughout this session"
   "fix: (gauge/u1-generators (:Y fermion) dim) ->
    (gauge/u1-generators (/ (:Y fermion) 2.0) dim). Added
    covariant-derivative-sm-photon-coupling-matches-e-times-Q: pure-photon
    field config (Z-component exactly zero), checks e_L coupling against
    -i*e*Q*psi exactly plus explicit check pre-fix value would be 1.5x too
    large -- regression strong enough to have caught this at original landing"
   "no other bugs found: complex/tensor core algebra, spinor's gamma
    matrices/Dirac equation, gauge's SU(2)/SU(3) generators+structure
    constants (self-interaction slot-order pattern independently reconfirmed
    correct for the ORIGINAL compact-group case too), CKM matrix (checked
    via independent 3-rotation matrix product, matched to floating-point
    noise), Higgs sector -- all matched independent derivation from physics
    literature"
   "coverage gaps noted but NOT fixed (not bugs, thin tests around
    already-correct code): gell-mann-nishijima-ok? tautological for 18/21
    fermion-table entries (only 3 independently spot-checked); photon-Z/
    mixing-matrix only tested for norm preservation (would not catch sign
    flip or A/Z swap); M_W=M_Z*cos(theta_W) and CKM unitarity tested at only
    1 fixed point each; covariant-derivative-sm's :color/:weak fermion-map
    shape never wired to fermion-content's :multiplet shape (part of why the
    hypercharge bug went unexercised against the real table); yang-mills-density
    test mislabels its n=0 branch as U(1) (real U(1) always has n=1)"
   "methodological consequence: THIRD real bug this session's independent-
    review discipline found in this repo (after PR #6, PR #11), and the
    first found in code that was NOT freshly-written -- the presumption that
    older/settled code is comparatively low-risk was wrong. This discipline
    (re-derive before reading, decompose combined systems and check the
    combination not just isolated pieces, independently re-verify proposed
    regression tests before trusting them) generalizes and should be
    considered for the rest of this repo's surface area, not treated as
    GTG-specific tooling"]
